        @* ================= TITLE CLEANER ================= *@
        <section class="panel" id="panel-title-cleaner" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-title-cleaner" hidden>

            <header class="page-head">
                @PageIcon("title-cleaner")
                <h1>Title Cleaner</h1>
                <span class="stamp" id="tc-stamp"></span>
            </header>

            <div class="card">
                <div class="uploader">
                    <div class="uploader-grid">
                        <label class="drop" id="tc-drop">
                            <span class="drop-title">Ürün dosyası</span>
                            <span class="drop-hint">Başlık + özellik kolonları &mdash; .xlsx or .csv</span>
                            <span class="drop-file"><span class="name"></span><span class="size"></span></span>
                            <input type="file" id="tc-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv" aria-label="Ürün dosyası" />
                        </label>
                    </div>

                    <div class="filter-bar">
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="tc-ruleset">Kural seti</label>
                            <select id="tc-ruleset"></select>
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="tc-set-name">Set adı</label>
                            <input type="text" id="tc-set-name" placeholder="Laptop" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="tc-title-column">Başlık kolonu</label>
                            <input type="text" id="tc-title-column" placeholder="Başlık" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="tc-decimal">Ondalık</label>
                            <select id="tc-decimal"
                                    title="Düzeltilen ondalıklı bir değer hücreye nasıl yazılsın — 15.6 mı, 15,6 mı. Eşleşmeyi etkilemez, yalnızca yazımı belirler.">
                                <option value=".">15.6</option>
                                <option value=",">15,6</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                        @* The one setting that removes text no column claimed, so it is off by
                           default and sits here rather than on a rule: it belongs to the whole set,
                           like the decimal separator.

                           A labelled chip rather than a bare checkbox in a .field — stretched by the
                           column layout that box came out 67px wide and empty, which reads as a text
                           input nobody filled in rather than as a switch. Same shape as the four
                           permission chips on a rule. *@
                        <label class="tc-check tc-setting" for="tc-collapse"
                               title="Başlıkta arka arkaya iki kez yazılmış aynı kelimenin ikincisini siler — &quot;Ideapad Ideapad Slim3&quot;. Rakam içeren tekrarlara asla dokunmaz: &quot;RTX 5070 8GB 8GB&quot; ekran kartının kendi belleğinin yanındaki sistem RAM'idir.">
                            <input type="checkbox" id="tc-collapse" />
                            <span>Tekrarı sil</span>
                        </label>
                    </div>

                    <div class="actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="tc-suggest">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Dosyadan kural öner</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="tc-preview">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Önizle</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>

                    <div class="alert" id="tc-alert" role="alert">
                        <strong>Error</strong>
                        <span class="msg"></span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="section-title">Kural seti</div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Hangi kolon başlıktan çıkarılacak</h3>

                <div id="tc-notes" hidden></div>

                @* A rule is a form with ten fields, one of which holds forty alias groups — not a
                   table row. As a table it needed eleven columns and a 720px minimum, so on any
                   ordinary screen the boxes were too narrow to read what was in them and the whole
                   thing scrolled sideways. Here the summary line stays scannable and the editing
                   happens underneath it, at full width. *@
                <div class="tc-rules" id="tc-rules">
                    <div class="tc-rules-head" aria-hidden="true">
                        <span>Kolon</span>
                        <span>Tip</span>
                        <span>Durum</span>
                        <span class="num">Eşleşme</span>
                    </div>
                    <div id="tc-rules-body"></div>
                </div>

                <p class="note">
                    <strong>RuleSet:</strong> <span id="tc-ruleset-status">yüklenmedi</span>
                    <br />
                    <strong>Referans listeleri:</strong> <span id="tc-reference-status">yüklenmedi</span>
                </p>

                @* A reference list supplies the spellings a cell does not carry — a processor
                   catalogue's "Intel Core Ultra 5 125H" against a column reading "Intel Core Ultra 5".
                   The column is asked for rather than guessed: a catalogue workbook carries source
                   URLs and family names beside the values.

                   Its own titled block rather than a second filter-bar: side by side with the rule
                   set's own settings the two looked like one thing, and the upload read as a setting
                   of the set it sits under. *@
                <div class="tc-subcard">
                    <h4>Referans listesi yükle</h4>
                    <p class="sub">Hücrede yazmayan uzun yazımlar için katalog &mdash; hücre &quot;Intel Core Ultra 5&quot;, başlık &quot;Ultra5 125H&quot;</p>
                    <div class="filter-bar is-plain">
                        @* "örn:" is not decoration. These two boxes sit empty and their examples name
                           the very values the list is usually built from, so without it they read as
                           already filled — the same trap the rule editor's boxes fell into. *@
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="tc-reference-name">Liste adı</label>
                            <input type="text" id="tc-reference-name" placeholder="örn: İşlemciler"
                                   title="Kural satırlarındaki Referans kutusunda bu adla görünür" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="tc-reference-column">Değer kolonu</label>
                            <input type="text" id="tc-reference-column" placeholder="örn: Tam İşlemci Adı"
                                   title="Değerlerin bulunduğu kolonun, çalışma kitabının başlık satırındaki adı. Her sayfada aranır." />
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="tc-reference-import"
                                    title="Değer kataloğu çalışma kitabı — her sayfada adı verilen kolon okunur">
